## Summary

Delivered a native **SwiftUI / Apple HIG** implementation of the web `TeslaChargingSessionsPage` (route `/tesla-charging-sessions`) at full parity, adaptive across macOS + iOS, committed as `b058e79ce`.

**Parity: 48/48 covered** (10 panels · 2 charts · 4 states · 32 strings)
- **Panels:** business-account info banner, vehicle-select + Tesla-refresh controls bar, 5 summary stat cards (Sessions/Energy/Cost/Avg-Cost·kWh/Peak-Power), Monthly-Charging-Cost chart, session-locations map, sessions table.
- **Charts:** `TSChartContainer` + `TSBarChart` (Swift Charts, no WKWebView).
- **States:** loading skeleton · per-section empty · retryable error · populated success — for every data source.
- **Strings:** all 32 ported verbatim from web `en.json` into `Localizable.xcstrings` (+ `route.teslaChargingSessions`).

**Architecture** mirrors the sibling Powershare P7: a `View` + `@Observable TeslaChargingSessionsPageModel` over a KMP-core data-source seam (one method per web hook — `useVehicles`/`useTeslaChargingSessions`/`useRefreshTeslaChargingSessions`); pure unit-tested derivations (monthly-cost, range filter, map points, CSV export); SI energy converted at the render boundary, peak power shown as the verbatim kW API field.

**Files:** 8 sources in `Sources/Features/Charging/`, 3 test files (25 tests), `AppRoute`/`TeslaSyncApp` nav registration, the string catalog, ledger rows, and the evidence log.

**Gate (all green):** `swiftlint --strict` 0/5806 · placeholder scan 0 · macOS app **BUILD SUCCEEDED** · **25/25 tests pass** · iOS-Simulator (arm64) app **BUILD SUCCEEDED**. Two pre-existing, out-of-scope, Xcode-26.5-incompatible files (`Input.Previews.swift`, `GDPRExportPageModelTests.swift`) were isolated via `EXCLUDED_SOURCE_FILE_NAMES` (build override, no source edits) and fully disclosed in the log — identical to the accepted Powershare precedent. Log ends `EXIT=0 / STATUS=DONE`.

Note on the environment: the host was under extreme multi-slot CPU contention (load peaked ~110), so the KMP framework + Xcode builds were slow, but all completed cleanly.

